        "subject": "LU-20565 tests: run sanity-ec with fewer OSTs",
        "message": "LU-20565 tests: run sanity-ec with fewer OSTs\n\nOn a filesystem with 4 OSTs, sanity-ec subtests 4e, 5b, 6d, 6e, 6f,\n7a, 23a, 23b, 23c, 24a, 25a, 26a and 28a would fail in \"lfs setstripe\"\nwith \"No space left on device (28)\", because they hard-code an EC 4+2\ngeometry and the raidset allocator needs 6 distinct OSTs for it.\n\nNone of these subtests depends on that geometry, so use the EC_ARG,\nEC_DSTRIPE and EC_CSTRIPE defaults that enable_ec() scales to OSTCOUNT\nfor the layout and the expected stripe counts.  Size the sanity-ec/26a\nfile and overwrite from EC_DSTRIPE so it still covers 5 full rows.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-ec\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-ec ostcount=4\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ie76079973f5ee62cb77888d448194913693ebbe5\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70175\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Marc Vef <mvef@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Keguang Xu <kxu@ddn.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
